{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Detailed_Explanation)_🚀⚡📊\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5 by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_6_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 6 by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Betty drives a truck to deliver packages in a neighborhood whose street map is shown below. Betty starts at the factory (labled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) and drives to location <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, before returning to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. What is the shortest distance, in blocks, she can drive to complete the route?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a367bb91ccfd9ca190ffa1534b6f06436102ec08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(20);  add(grid(8,6));  path w = circle((0,0),0.4);  fill(w, white); draw(w); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,0));  fill(shift((2,4)) * w, white); draw(shift((2,4)) * w); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(2,4));  fill(shift((7,3)) * w, white); draw(shift((7,3)) * w); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(7,3));  fill(shift((6,5)) * w, white); draw(shift((6,5)) * w); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(6,5));  draw((6,-0.2)--(7,-0.2), EndArrow(3)); draw((7,-0.2)--(6,-0.2), EndArrow(3)); draw(shift(6.5, -0.48) * scale(0.03) * texpath(&quot;1 block&quot;));  draw((8.2,1)--(8.2,2), EndArrow(3)); draw((8.2,2)--(8.2,1), EndArrow(3)); draw(shift(8.88, 1.5) * scale(0.03) * texpath(&quot;1 block&quot;)); [/asy]\" width=\"328\" height=\"222\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5dec7bae4ee342cef90d6dea58fcb4cb9392c758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 23 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 26\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each shortest possible path from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> follows the edges of the rectangle. The following path outlines a path of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a6c7874dcb6218a9c119821950da1be38f8e59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" /> units:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/930173277b92d2c7a4f876d1f76eb42007e87e1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(20);  add(grid(8,6)); draw((6,5)--(7,5)--(7,0)--(0,0)--(0,4)--(2,4)--(2,5)--cycle,green);  path w = circle((0,0),0.4);  fill(w, white); draw(w); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,0));  fill(shift((2,4)) * w, white); draw(shift((2,4)) * w); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(2,4));  fill(shift((7,3)) * w, white); draw(shift((7,3)) * w); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(7,3));  fill(shift((6,5)) * w, white); draw(shift((6,5)) * w); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(6,5)); [/asy]\" width=\"282\" height=\"215\" />\n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zhenghua\" title=\"Zhenghua\">zhenghua</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the shortest distance using a line diagonally from one point to the other, creating a sort of slope, then find the sum of rise and run of the slope, which happens to be the shortest distance, repeat this process until you get back to Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and you should get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd39ed211367434adaacc535ce487e8067ae06f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 1 + 3 + 7 + 4 + 2 + 1 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"230\" height=\"15\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a6c7874dcb6218a9c119821950da1be38f8e59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n~Imhappy62789\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the shortest distance Betty drives, we apply Taxicab Geometry (also known as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f22b669e4803ae525cf8120ca251e2eab025872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> metric). In a grid system, the distance between any two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/991c93bf3b5f578663c6c139c34f79cc70713969.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1, y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574cd26ba0fbfb46272d82eb95420c5fdbc53546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2, y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb94acac4da18010b35ebe0a2722fab0748a6f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = |x_1 - x_2| + |y_1 - y_2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Let the bottom-left corner of the grid be the origin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Based on the provided map, we assign coordinates to the given locations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943df464f6bacb9e19cddd41029163b289104bb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/178bf4b97eb4251b5c07942b8fd763cf4f807d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (2, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664c94d10f04b5b72197941554da9fa45d7408de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F = (6, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a18b77050822cc70884d4b9b54a0c7d5eea6695c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (7, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nBetty's route follows the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7a8239cbc65e34bc449e089fd2da18f7b71b33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F \\to A \\to B \\to C \\to F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"186\" height=\"14\" />. We calculate the Manhattan distance for each leg of the journey:\n</p><p>F (6, 5) to A (7, 3):  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbd39623cd8979bf2bbb70a81dc85dbf2d789200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|6 - 7| + |5 - 3| = 1 + 2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>A( 7, 3) to B (0, 0):  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/937d7397f40e6f849958a872ec281c676d0e4416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|7 - 0| + |3 - 0| = 7 + 3 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"232\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>B (0, 0) to C (2, 4):  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8bd242254ebb3935b564c12a781e0c8f0674087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|0 - 2| + |0 - 4| = 2 + 4 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>C (2, 4) to F (6, 5):  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a093e69460b13b2ebf17ccbe7b6d243f807532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|2 - 6| + |4 - 5| = 4 + 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe total shortest distance is the sum of these segments:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5de54278e6fa755eaf84be7802cb38f1bf6bb72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 + 10 + 6 + 5 = 24\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The shortest distance Betty can drive to complete the route is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d2cca89d5aa7ed0a9130ce403b8bf8a23a869c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~HeirX_on_TT\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/rjd0gigUsd0\">~Thesmartgreekmathdude</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5Jak6VUDojA\">https://youtu.be/5Jak6VUDojA</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math\">Video Solution by Continuum Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Continuum Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mBYYaoPQsbs&amp;t=151\">https://youtu.be/mBYYaoPQsbs&amp;t=151</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=petj-pgcGGwx62qv&amp;t=633\">https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=petj-pgcGGwx62qv&amp;t=633</a>\n~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Detailed_Explanation.29_.F0.9F.9A.80.E2.9A.A1.F0.9F.93.8A\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Detailed_Explanation)_🚀⚡📊\">Video Solution 2 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (Detailed Explanation) 🚀⚡📊\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n6M3y_1dsOk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n6M3y_1dsOk</a>\n</p><p>~ ChillThingz&#160;:)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=2TfegPRg-_k1DEcz&amp;t=257\">https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=2TfegPRg-_k1DEcz&amp;t=257</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_5_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution 5 by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 5 by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988\">https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_6_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution 6 by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.p